# Humility takes Necrotic Ooze's "it has all activated abilities of all creature cards in all graveyards" in layer 6 (CR
# 613.1f), and with it every ability that ability would give: the Ooze's grant depends on Humility's effect, which applies
# first (CR 613.8a), though the Ooze came first. Walking Ballista is in Bot1's graveyard (cast for X = 0 on turn 1), and on
# turn 5, with four mana open, the Ooze offers neither of its abilities (the refusal) - the positive control is
# necrotic-ooze-has-the-activated-abilities-of-a-creature-card-in-an-opponents-graveyard, where the same {4} is activated.
